n verification\n\n**Technologies:** FastAPI, Python\n\n**Depends on:** `Auth Service`, `Core Service`\n\n### Application Layer\n\n#### Auth Service (`COMP-auth-service`)\n\nHandles user authentication and authorization.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- User registration/login\n- JWT token management\n- OAuth2 integration\n- RBAC enforcement\n\n**Technologies:** FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, PyJWT\n\n**Depends on:** `PostgreSQL`, `Redis`\n\n#### Core Service (`COMP-core-service`)\n\nCore business logic and workflow orchestration.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Workflow execution\n- Event processing\n- State management\n- Agent coordination\n\n**Technologies:** FastAPI, LangGraph, Celery\n\n**Depends on:** `PostgreSQL`, `Redis`, `Message Queue`\n\n#### Governance Service (`COMP-governance-service`)\n\nPolicy evaluation and compliance checking.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- OPA policy evaluation\n- Release gate management\n- Compliance reporting\n- Audit logging\n\n**Technologies:** FastAPI, OPA, Rego\n\n**Depends on:** `PostgreSQL`\n\n### Domain Layer\n\n#### Specification Engine (`COMP-specification-engine`)\n\nGenerates and validates specification artifacts.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Requirements management\n- Spec validation\n- Version control\n- Diff generation\n\n**Technologies:** Python, PyYAML\n\n**Depends on:** `Core Service`\n\n#### Architecture Engine (`COMP-architecture-engine`)\n\nGenerates architecture artifacts and detects drift.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Component modeling\n- ADR management\n- Drift detection\n- Diagram generation\n\n**Technologies:** Python, Mermaid\n\n**Depends on:** `Core Service`\n\n#### Test Engine (`COMP-test-engine`)\n\nGenerates test plans and strategies.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Test plan generation\n- Traceability mapping\n- Coverage analysis\n\n**Technologies:** Python, pytest\n\n**Depends on:** `Core Service`, `Specification Engine`\n\n### Infrastructure Layer\n\n#### PostgreSQL (`COMP-postgresql`)\n\nPrimary relational database.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Data persistence\n- Transaction management\n- Migration support\n\n**Technologies:** PostgreSQL, Alembic\n\n#### Redis (`COMP-redis`)\n\nIn-memory cache and message broker.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Session caching\n- Rate limiting counters\n- Pub/sub messaging\n\n**Technologies:** Redis\n\n#### Message Queue (`COMP-message-queue`)\n\nAsync message processing.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Task queuing\n- Event broadcasting\n- Dead letter handling\n\n**Technologies:** Redis Streams, RabbitMQ\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Constraints\n\n| ID | Name | Enforcement | Description |\n|----|------|-------------|-------------|\n| CONST-no-direct-db-access | No Direct DB Access | review | Services must not directly access another service's database. |\n| CONST-api-versioning | API Versioning | build_time | All API endpoints must include version in URL path. |\n| CONST-auth-required | Auth Required | build_time | All API endpoints except health check require authentication. |\n| CONST-no-circular-dependencies | No Circular Dependencies | build_time | Service dependency graph must be acyclic. |\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Fitness Functions\n\n| ID | Name | Metric | Threshold | Current | Status |\n|----|------|--------|-----------|---------|--------|\n| FF-api-response-time | API Response Time | latency_p95_ms | <= 200 | None | ❓ unknown |\n| FF-test-coverage | Test Coverage | coverage_percent | >= 80 | None | ❓ unknown |\n| FF-dependency-count | Dependency Count | dependency_count | <= 5 | None | ❓ unknown |\n| FF-service-count | Service Count | service_count | <= 20 | None | ❓ unknown |\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Decision Records\n\n### ADR-001: Microservices Architecture\n\n**Status:** accepted\n\n**Context:** The system needs to support independent deployment and scaling of different capabilities.\n\n**Decision:** Adopt a microservices architecture with clear service boundaries and API contracts.\n\n**Consequences:**\n- Independent deployment per service\n- Technology flexibility per service\n- Increased operational complexity\n- Network latency between services\n\n**Alternatives Considered:**\n- Monolithic architecture\n- Serverless functions\n\n### ADR-002: PostgreSQL as Primary Database\n\n**Status:** accepted\n\n**Context:** The system requires ACID compliance and complex query support for workflow state.\n\n**Decision:** Use PostgreSQL as the primary relational database with SQLAlchemy ORM.\n\n**Consequences:**\n- ACID transactions\n- Rich query language\n- Mature ecosystem\n- Vertical scaling limits\n\n**Alternatives Considered:**\n- MongoDB\n- MySQL\n- CockroachDB\n\n### ADR-003: LangGraph for Workflow Orchestration\n\n**Status:** accepted\n\n**Context:** Complex multi-step workflows with branching, retries, and state management are required.\n\n**Decision:** Use LangGraph for workflow orchestration with checkpoint-based state management.\n\n**Consequences:**\n- Visual workflow representation\n- Built-in checkpointing\n- Conditional routing\n- LangChain ecosystem coupling\n\n**Alternatives Considered:**\n- Airflow\n- Prefect\n- Custom state machine\n\n### ADR-004: OPA for Governance Policies\n\n**Status:** accepted\n\n**Context:** Governance policies need to be declarative, testable, and separable from application code.\n\n**Decision:** Use Open Policy Agent (OPA) with Rego for all governance policy evaluation.\n\n**Consequences:**\n- Declarative policies\n- Testable rules\n- Policy-as-code\n- Performance overhead of external evaluation\n\n**Alternatives Considered:**\n- Custom rule engine\n- Hardcoded checks\n\n### ADR-005: WebSocket for Real-time Updates\n\n**Status:** accepted\n\n**Context:** The control tower UI requires real-time updates for workflow progress and events.\n\n**Decision:** Use WebSocket connections with automatic reconnection for live event streaming.\n\n**Consequences:**\n- Low-latency updates\n- Bidirectional communication\n- Connection management complexity\n\n**Alternatives Considered:**\n- Server-Sent Events\n- Polling\n- Long polling\n	{"sequence": "sequenceDiagram\\n    participant Client\\n    participant API\\n    participant Service\\n    participant Database\\n\\n    Client->>API: HTTP Request\\n    API->>Service: Process Request\\n    Service->>Database: Query Data\\n    Database-->>Service: Result\\n    Service-->>API: Response\\n    API-->>Client: HTTP Response", "component": "graph TD\\n    COMP_api_gateway[\\"API Gateway<br/><small>gateway</small>\\"]\\n    COMP_auth_service[\\"Auth Service<br/><small>service</small>\\"]\\n    COMP_core_service[\\"Core Service<br/><small>service</small>\\"]\\n    COMP_governance_service[\\"Governance Service<br/><small>service</small>\\"]\\n    COMP_specification_engine[\\"Specification Engine<br/><small>module</small>\\"]\\n    COMP_architecture_engine[\\"Architecture Engine<br/><small>module</small>\\"]\\n    COMP_test_engine[\\"Test Engine<br/><small>module</small>\\"]\\n    COMP_postgresql[\\"PostgreSQL<br/><small>database</small>\\"]\\n    COMP_redis[\\"Redis<br/><small>cache</small>\\"]\\n    COMP_message_queue[\\"Message Queue<br/><small>queue</small>\\"]\\n    COMP_api_gateway --> Auth Service\\n    COMP_api_gateway --> Core Service\\n    COMP_auth_service --> PostgreSQL\\n    COMP_auth_service --> Redis\\n    COMP_core_service --> PostgreSQL\\n    COMP_core_service --> Redis\\n    COMP_core_service --> Message Queue\\n    COMP_governance_service --> PostgreSQL\\n    COMP_specification_engine --> Core Service\\n    COMP_architecture_engine --> Core Service\\n    COMP_test_engine --> Core Service\\n    COMP_test_engine --> Specification Engine", "deployment": "graph LR\\n    subgraph Client Tier\\n        Web[Web Browser]\\n        Mobile[Mobile App]\\n    end\\n\\n    subgraph Application Tier\\n        API[API Gateway]\\n        Auth[Auth Service]\\n        Core[Core Service]\\n    end\\n\\n    subgraph Data Tier\\n        DB[(PostgreSQL)]\\n        Cache[(Redis)]\\n        Queue[Message Queue]\\n    end\\n\\n    Web --> API\\n    Mobile --> API\\n    API --> Auth\\n    API --> Core\\n    Core --> DB\\n    Core --> Cache\\n    Core --> Queue"}	[{"id": "001", "title": "Microservices Architecture", "status": "accepted", "context": "The system needs to support independent deployment and scaling of different capabilities.", "decision": "Adopt a microservices architecture with clear service boundaries and API contracts.", "created_at": "2026-05-15T05:07:11.027547+00:00", "alternatives": ["Monolithic architecture", "Serverless functions"], "consequences": ["Independent deployment per service", "Technology flexibility per service", "Increased operational complexity", "Network latency between services"]}, {"id": "002", "title": "PostgreSQL as Primary Database", "status": "accepted", "context": "The system requires ACID compliance and complex query support for workflow state.", "decision": "Use PostgreSQL as the primary relational database with SQLAlchemy ORM.", "created_at": "2026-05-15T05:07:11.027550+00:00", "alternatives": ["MongoDB", "MySQL", "CockroachDB"], "consequences": ["ACID transactions", "Rich query language", "Mature ecosystem", "Vertical scaling limits"]}, {"id": "003", "title": "LangGraph for Workflow Orchestration", "status": "accepted", "context": "Complex multi-step workflows with branching, retries, and state management are required.", "decision": "Use LangGraph for workflow orchestration with checkpoint-based state management.", "created_at": "2026-05-15T05:07:11.027552+00:00", "alternatives": ["Airflow", "Prefect", "Custom state machine"], "consequences": ["Visual workflow representation", "Built-in checkpointing", "Conditional routing", "LangChain ecosystem coupling"]}, {"id": "004", "title": "OPA for Governance Policies", "status": "accepted", "context": "Governance policies need to be declarative, testable, and separable from application code.", "decision": "Use Open Policy Agent (OPA) with Rego for all governance policy evaluation.", "creat