c4ec7d3c-25b6-4445-ad93-f1af63e4c86c	\N	b1058357-9832-4796-8718-c96169725359	architecture.md	architecture	# Architecture Document\n\n**Run ID:** `b1058357-9832-4796-8718-c96169725359`\n**Project ID:** `b7c7ab14-9d35-4fec-a9be-b876e38d16b9`\n**Generated:** 2026-05-14T18:48:05.497820+00:00\n\n---\n\n## System Overview\n\nThis system follows a **microservices architecture** with 10 components.\n\n## Architecture Layers\n\n### Presentation Layer\n\n#### API Gateway (`COMP-api-gateway`)\n\nEntry point for all client requests. Handles routing, rate limiting, and authentication.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Route requests to services\n- Rate limiting\n- Request validation\n- Auth token verification\n\n**Technologies:** FastAPI, Python\n\n**Depends on:** `Auth Service`, `Core Service`\n\n### Application Layer\n\n#### Auth Service (`COMP-auth-service`)\n\nHandles user authentication and authorization.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- User registration/login\n- JWT token management\n- OAuth2 integration\n- RBAC enforcement\n\n**Technologies:** FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, PyJWT\n\n**Depends on:** `PostgreSQL`, `Redis`\n\n#### Core Service (`COMP-core-service`)\n\nCore business logic and workflow orchestration.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Workflow execution\n- Event processing\n- State management\n- Agent coordination\n\n**Technologies:** FastAPI, LangGraph, Celery\n\n**Depends on:** `PostgreSQL`, `Redis`, `Message Queue`\n\n#### Governance Service (`COMP-governance-service`)\n\nPolicy evaluation and compliance checking.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- OPA policy evaluation\n- Release gate management\n- Compliance reporting\n- Audit logging\n\n**Technologies:** FastAPI, OPA, Rego\n\n**Depends on:** `PostgreSQL`\n\n### Domain Layer\n\n#### Specification Engine (`COMP-specification-engine`)\n\nGenerates and validates specification artifacts.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Requirements management\n- Spec validation\n- Version control\n- Diff generation\n\n**Technologies:** Python, PyYAML\n\n**Depends on:** `Core Service`\n\n#### Architecture Engine (`COMP-architecture-engine`)\n\nGenerates architecture artifacts and detects drift.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Component modeling\n- ADR management\n- Drift detection\n- Diagram generation\n\n**Technologies:** Python, Mermaid\n\n**Depends on:** `Core Service`\n\n#### Test Engine (`COMP-test-engine`)\n\nGenerates test plans and strategies.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Test plan generation\n- Traceability mapping\n- Coverage analysis\n\n**Technologies:** Python, pytest\n\n**Depends on:** `Core Service`, `Specification Engine`\n\n### Infrastructure Layer\n\n#### PostgreSQL (`COMP-postgresql`)\n\nPrimary relational database.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Data persistence\n- Transaction management\n- Migration support\n\n**Technologies:** PostgreSQL, Alembic\n\n#### Redis (`COMP-redis`)\n\nIn-memory cache and message broker.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Session caching\n- Rate limiting counters\n- Pub/sub messaging\n\n**Technologies:** Redis\n\n#### Message Queue (`COMP-message-queue`)\n\nAsync message processing.\n\n**Responsibilities:**\n- Task queuing\n- Event broadcasting\n- Dead letter handling\n\n**Technologies:** Redis Streams, RabbitMQ\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Constraints\n\n| ID | Name | Enforcement | Description |\n|----|------|-------------|-------------|\n| CONST-no-direct-db-access | No Direct DB Access | review | Services must not directly access another service's database. |\n| CONST-api-versioning | API Versioning | build_time | All API endpoints must include version in URL path. |\n| CONST-auth-required | Auth Required | build_time | All API endpoints except health check require authentication. |\n| CONST-no-circular-dependencies | No Circular Dependencies | build_time | Service dependency graph must be acyclic. |\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Fitness Functions\n\n| ID | Name | Metric | Threshold | Current | Status |\n|----|------|--------|-----------|---------|--------|\n| FF-api-response-time | API Response Time | latency_p95_ms | <= 200 | None | ❓ unknown |\n| FF-test-coverage | Test Coverage | coverage_percent | >= 80 | None | ❓ unknown |\n| FF-dependency-count | Dependency Count | dependency_count | <= 5 | None | ❓ unknown |\n| FF-service-count | Service Count | service_count | <= 20 | None | ❓ unknown |\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Decision Records\n\n### ADR-001: Microservices Architecture\n\n**Status:** accepted\n\n**Context:** The system needs to support independent deployment and scaling of different capabilities.\n\n**Decision:** Adopt a microservices architecture with clear service boundaries and API contracts.\n\n**Consequences:**\n- Independent deployment per service\n- Technology flexibility per service\n- Increased operational complexity\n- Network latency between services\n\n**Alternatives Considered:**\n- Monolithic architecture\n- Serverless functions\n\n### ADR-002: PostgreSQL as Primary Database\n\n**Status:** accepted\n\n**Context:** The system requires ACID compliance and complex query support for workflow state.\n\n**Decision:** Use PostgreSQL as the primary relational database with SQLAlchemy ORM.\n\n**Consequences:**\n- ACID transactions\n- Rich query language\n- Mature ecosystem\n- Vertical scaling limits\n\n**Alternatives Considered:**\n- MongoDB\n- MySQL\n- CockroachDB\n\n### ADR-003: LangGraph for Workflow Orchestration\n\n**Status:** accepted\n\n**Context:** Complex multi-step workflows with branching, retries, and state management are required.\n\n**Decision:** Use LangGraph for workflow orchestration with checkpoint-based state management.\n\n**Consequences:**\n- Visual workflow representation\n- Built-in checkpointing\n- Conditional routing\n- LangChain ecosystem coupling\n\n**Alternatives Considered:**\n- Airflow\n- Prefect\n- Custom state machine\n\n### ADR-004: OPA for Governance Policies\n\n**Status:** accepted\n\n**Context:** Governance policies need to be declarative, testable, and separable from application code.\n\n**Decision:** Use Open Policy Agent (OPA) with Rego for all governance policy evaluation.\n\n**Consequences:**\n- Declarative policies\n- Testable rules\n- Policy-as-code\n- Performance overhead of external evaluation\n\n**Alternatives Considered:**\n- Custom rule engine\n- Hardcoded checks\n\n### ADR-005: WebSocket for Real-time Updates\n\n**Status:** accepted\n\n**Context:** The control tower UI requires real-time updates for workflow progress and events.\n\n**Decision:** Use WebSocket connections with automatic reconnection for live event streaming.\n\n**Consequences:**\n- Low-latency updates\n- Bidirectional communication\n- Connection management complexity\n\n**Alternatives Considered:**\n- Server-Sent Events\n- Polling\n- Long polling\n	/tmp/cortex-artifacts/b1058357-9832-4796-8718-c96169725359/architecture.md	1	f	f	{"subdir": "", "phase_name": "architecture", "size_bytes": 6359, "content_hash": "76a110da87af6dce54b0792c625aeb87aee891beb8be081692b6218840ac6e07", "source_engine": "architecture-engine", "parent_artifact_id": null}	2026-05-14 18:48:05.524976+00	architecture	\N	\N
